      "description": "The SMTP protocol allows a server to formally reject a mail session while still allowing the initial connection: a 554 response MAY be given in the initial connection opening message instead of the 220. A server taking this approach MUST still wait for the client to send a QUIT before closing the connection and SHOULD respond to any intervening commands with '503 bad sequence of commands'.",
